; Disables Node's automatic IPv4/IPv6 address selection ("happy eyeballs").
;
; Node races the A and AAAA records from DNS at once. On networks where IPv6
; is advertised but not actually routable (common on some routers, VPNs and
; mobile hotspots), Node latches onto the dead IPv6 address and the whole
; request times out -- even though a perfectly good IPv4 address was available.
; That made every Neon query fail with ConnectTimeoutError and left the
; storefront showing an empty catalogue.
;
; Forcing IPv4-first resolution avoids that. Remove this file once IPv6
; connectivity works properly on the machine running the app.
node-options=--no-network-family-autoselection